    "file": "EC2022.pdf",
    "page": 51,
    "prompt": "An iid real source has density proportional to x+2 on −2≤x≤0, and constant at the same height f(0) on 0<x≤1; it is zero elsewhere. A 1-bit quantizer maps positive samples to α and others to β. For minimum MSE reproduction levels α*,β*, find α*−β* to two decimal places.",
    "answer": "1.15 to 1.18",
    "steps": [
      "Optimal squared-error reconstruction values are conditional means in each fixed quantization region.",
      "The positive side is uniform over [0,1], so α*=1/2.",
      "The negative side is a triangular density increasing from −2 to 0, with mean β*=(−2+0+0)/3=−2/3.",
      "Thus α*−β*=1/2+2/3=7/6≈1.17."
    ],
    "officialKey": "1.15:1.18",
    "response": {
      "type": "NAT"
    },
