    "prompt": "An electrostatic displacement field is D(x,y,z)=(x³ i+y³ j+xy² k) C/m². Find enclosed charge in the unit cube centered at the origin, with vertices (±.5,±.5,±.5) m, to two decimal places.",
    "answer": "0.48 to 0.52",
    "steps": [
      "Gauss’s law in differential form gives charge density ρv=∇·D=3x²+3y².",
      "Over the cube, each of the x² and y² terms integrates to ∫(−.5 to .5)u²du=1/12, with unit lengths in the other coordinates.",
      "Thus enclosed charge is 3(1/12+1/12)=.50 C."
    ],
    "officialKey": "0.48:0.52",
    "response": {
      "type": "NAT"
    }
